Revision history for Search-Tantivy

0.05  2026-11-22
      - Sorting by numeric, date and string fields: search option
        sort => 'field' / '-field'. New string fields are sortable.
      - date field type (epoch seconds, YYYY-MM-DD, RFC 3339; range queries).
      - add_many(\@docs) adds a batch in one call.
      - search option return_fields to return only some stored fields.
      - Uses Cpanel::JSON::XS or JSON::XS when installed (big documents
        decode 50x faster than with JSON::PP); SEARCH_TANTIVY_JSON overrides.
      - examples/bench: indexing and query speed against SQLite FTS5 and
        Lucy, whichever are installed.

0.04  2026-11-22
      - search() option offset, search_page() returning hits plus the total
        number of matches, and count().
      - Typo tolerance: search option fuzzy => 1|2. Exact matches rank first;
        snippets highlight the words that matched.
      - fork() safety: an object that wrote no longer hangs or releases the
        parent's write lock when destroyed in a child; writing there croaks.
        Objects are not cloned into new threads (would double free).
      - examples/podsearch: --fuzzy, total number of matches.

0.03  2026-11-22
      - Language-aware text fields: stemming for 19 languages incl. Polish
        (language option, or shorthand type 'text:pl'), and ascii_folding.
      - reload() to see commits made by other processes.
      - search() options default_operator (AND/OR) and boost (per field).
      - examples/podsearch: index and search the POD of everything in @INC;
        exact word forms rank above stemmed look-alikes, --exact disables stemming.

0.02  2026-11-21
      - Add AI_DISCLOSURE.md.

0.01  2026-11-21
      - First version: create/open index, add, commit, search, num_docs.
      - Field types text, string, u64, i64, f64; stored or index-only.
      - delete() and update() by an exact string or numeric key.
      - Highlighted, HTML-escaped snippets in search results
        (snippets, snippet_chars, highlight options).
      - GitHub Actions CI: Linux and macOS, Perl 5.26 and 5.40.
      - Prebuilt, checksum-verified libraries for Linux (x86_64/aarch64,
        glibc and musl), macOS and Windows: no Rust needed to install.
